  "result": "Fixed. The command now prints **27.06**, and all 6 tests pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py:9` padded the decimal part on the wrong side. `\"12.5\"` split into whole `\"12\"` and fraction `\"5\"`, and `\"5\".rjust(2, \"0\")` turned the fraction into `\"05\"`. So $12.50 was read as 1205 cents instead of 1250. The fix is one line: pad on the right with `frac.ljust(2, \"0\")`, so `\"5\"` becomes `\"50\"`.\n\n**Check:** 1250 \u00d7 2 = 2500 cents, plus 8.25% tax (206 cents) = 2706, which prints as 27.06.\n\nThe tests passed before the fix too, because none of them uses a price with a single decimal place. It's worth adding a test like `to_cents(\"12.5\") == 1250`; I can add it if you want.",
